  "body": "Follow-up from the review of PR #502 (#303).\n\n`EdgeBreak::is_sane` (`crates/cl/src/cl/edge_break.rs`) and the project loader accept any finite, positive `depth`. The sim's edge-break credit (`crates/sim/src/stock_sim/edge_break.rs`) forgives convicted columns down to `edge_z - depth + slope*d`, within the declared plan width. A record hand-edited (or corrupted) to a large depth therefore widens the band in which a real gouge is forgiven. Generated records are bounded by the operation's own parameters, so this only reaches a document through the file.\n\n**Fix:** bound the record at load and in `is_sane`. The depth must not exceed the declaring operation's own chamfer/deburr depth (or a stated absolute cap, e.g. the tool's flute length), and the width must be consistent with the depth and slope. A record outside the bound is dropped by name, the same fail-closed path as a lattice mismatch: the program is then judged against the sharp model.\n\nDone means: a project whose edge-break record states an inflated depth loads with that record dropped and a named note, and the program verdict convicts a cut below the operation's real depth. Pinned by a sim or app test.\n\nPart of #303.\n",
